The auto-rickshaw arrives near Deepa's house.
I give the driver one hundred rupees.
He gives back twenty rupees.
I open the gate and walk into the courtyard of the house.
I think that this is a very beautiful house.
I go near the door and ring the bell.
Deepa opens the door quickly.
She smiles at me happily.
"Welcome Maya!"
"Come inside," Deepa says.
I step inside.
"You can put your bag here," Deepa says.
I give her the box of sweets.
"What is this, Maya?" Deepa asks.
"This is some halwa for us to eat," I say.
"Prakash said that this bakery is very good."
"Oh!"
"Prakash likes this bakery very much," Deepa says with a laugh.
"We can eat this after dinner."
I think that today's evening will be very nice.
